gcmove 1 fps:30
build {
}
# GRAPHCODE MOVE: THE HUMAN BODY'S POSE PRESETS, shipped with the Move plugin. Do not build this file: name it from your own
# file's header with  presets:/GraphCodeMove/Presets/Human/HumanBody  and call its presets ($Stance(...), $Back(...), ...) in your
# clips. Your file keeps its own character:, part:, ik_rig:, controls:, physics_asset: and into: lines. The bone names are a
# MetaHuman body's; the rig_ numbers were measured on the MetaHuman ClothedReference body, and another body passes its own.
# README.md beside this file says how to start; the guide is Plugins/GraphCode/Docs/Guides/MOVE-PARAMETRIC-POSES.md.
#
# A preset is a parameterised pose for one body part: Name = pose(value=default, ...) { lines }, called $Name(value=...).
# A value not written is none: its lines are not written (each optional fact sits in its own if ($x != none) { }); a default
# that is a formula follows the values it reads, and is none when one of them is. Degrees count from the figure: raise 0 straight
# down, 90 level, 180 up; azimuth 0 ahead, 90 out to the limb's own side, 180 behind, below 0 across; tipped forward, to the
# right and turned to the right are positive (lean, nod; side, tilt, chest_tilt; turn, twist). A sided preset takes left=true,
# right=true; a side written false writes none of its lines, so uneven sides are two calls. Every number of this skeleton is a
# rig_ value with its default; another skeleton overrides those. Helpers (marked) only carry arithmetic for the preset above them.
# RANGES: every value an author writes carries its range
# beside it as two parameters, x_min and x_max: a number outside is refused by name, x=max / x=min mean the end, and a call may
# widen an end ($Back(lean=75, lean_max=75)). An end is this body's measured stop where one was found, a formula where the end
# follows another value (Back's lean grows with the hunch), else the value's own scale.

# What the presets aim from (each bone along its length; the face is the head bone's +Y, its up +X).
Face = frame(bone=head, toward=+Y, up=+X)
# Three names for the neck and head: the build holds one aim per name, and Head's two aims and its look are separate holds.
LookH = bones(neck_01, neck_02, head)
LookL = bones(neck_01, neck_02, head)
Look = bones(neck_01, neck_02, head)
UpperArmR = frame(bone=upperarm_r, toward=lowerarm_r)
UpperArmL = frame(bone=upperarm_l, toward=lowerarm_l)
# a forearm's frame: along the forearm, its up the PALM's normal (lowerarm +Z on the right, -Z on the left)
ForeR = frame(bone=lowerarm_r, toward=-X, up=Z)
ForeL = frame(bone=lowerarm_l, toward=X, up=-Z)
ThighR = frame(bone=thigh_r, toward=calf_r)
ThighL = frame(bone=thigh_l, toward=calf_l)
ShinR = frame(bone=calf_r, toward=foot_r)
ShinL = frame(bone=calf_l, toward=foot_l)
FootR = frame(bone=foot_r, toward=ball_r)
FootL = frame(bone=foot_l, toward=ball_l)
ToesR = frame(bone=ball_r, toward=indextoe_02_r)
ToesL = frame(bone=ball_l, toward=indextoe_02_l)

# =====================================================================================================================
# BACK (first layer, not sided): the hinge at the hips (the pelvis's forward tilt) and the spine's shape (spine_01..05: fold,
# side, twist). Plain swings, no aim. The legs and arms are not Back's: a standing pose writes Stance, and a side lean writes
# the arms (a hanging hand meets the thigh at a side lean of about 10).
#  lean        degrees, 0 = the line from the middle of the two hip joints to neck_01 VERTICAL; positive tipped forward,
#              below 0 back. Not written: no hinge, unless the back's shape is written (round, lumbar or thoracic): then the
#              line keeps its rest tilt (rig_rest_tilt, -3.8: it stands a little back) and the pelvis tucks under the curve.
#              The line tips by lean for any shape (the hinge is lean less the curve's own tip). Measured range: see below.
#  round       -1..1, 0 = the rest shape: 1 every spine joint at its forward stop (curled), -1 at its back stop (arched).
#              Not written, follows lean: forward 0.95 * (1 - (1 - lean/100)^1.74), backward -0.62 * |lean| / 19, clamped -1..1
#              (lean 45 -> 0.62; 25 -> 0.37; -10 -> -0.33). round=0 written is a straight back on purpose (a formal bow).
#  lumbar      -1..1, the lower back's shape alone: spine_01, spine_02, spine_03. Not written, follows round.
#  thoracic    -1..1, the upper back's shape alone: spine_04, spine_05. Not written, follows round.
#              Why that split: the rig's own twist room is 3 / 3 / 3 / 12.5 / 12.5 (a lumbar spine barely turns, a thoracic one
#              does), and at rest spine_01..03 stand at 99, 106, 114 cm, below the ribs, spine_04 and 05 at 123 and 136 cm.
#  side        degrees, the line tipped to the figure's RIGHT (below 0 left), by the spine alone, counted from the pelvis (a
#              Hips.hike tips the pelvis under it). Not written: not asked (0 when chest_tilt alone is written).
#  chest_tilt  degrees, the shoulder line rolled to the RIGHT against the pelvis. Not written, follows side * rig_chest_ratio
#              (1.558: the five joints bent alike); written, the lower and upper back share the bend so the line still tips
#              by side. The rig gives the upper back 6 a joint (rig_side_room), so the shoulders' roll against the line is held
#              there: chest_tilt alone reaches about 6; side=8, chest_tilt=0 keeps the line at 8 and the roll stops at about 4.
#  twist       degrees, the shoulders turned to the figure's RIGHT against the hips (left shoulder forward), shared as the
#              rig's twist room is. Not written: not asked.
#  rig_flex, rig_extend   each spine joint's room from rest forward / back (18, 6); rig_twist1..5 their twist room;
#  rig_l0..5, rig_b0..5   the six segments hip-middle -> spine_01 -> ... -> spine_05 -> neck_01: length cm, rest tilt forward
#              degrees, read at rest; rig_rest_tilt the line's rest tilt (-3.80, back); rig_chest_ratio as above.
#  Measured (feet held, dry runs of 17 Nov): lean -33.8 .. 100 built exact to 0.06 (the hip's extension ends it near -38
#              from vertical; forward the corrected pelvis (135) lets the thigh decide, not built past 100); round -1 .. 1 at
#              lean 30 (the line 30.06 / 30.00); at lean 0 a round past about 0.65 lifts held feet (hip extension); side
#              -18.81 .. 18.81 (each joint's 6, the build names it past); twist -33.67 .. 33.67; chest_tilt about -6 .. 6 at side 0.
#  Worked values (built): a lean that rounds as it goes $Back(lean=45) -> line 45.00, round 0.614; a hunch
#              $Back(lean=45, round=0.8, side=8) -> 45.11 / 8.01; a slouch $Back(round=0.5) -> the line stays -3.80, the pelvis
#              tucks 29.05; a sway-back $Back(lean=20, lumbar=-0.7, thoracic=0.6) -> 20.00.
Back = pose(lean=none, lean_min=$rig_hinge_back + $rig_rest_tilt + (atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1 + (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2 + 2 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + 2 * (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend)), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1 + (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2 + 2 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + 2 * (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend))) - atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))), lean_max=min($rig_hinge_forward + $rig_rest_tilt + (atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1 + (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2 + 2 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + 2 * (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend)), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1 + (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2 + 2 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend)) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5 + 3 * (max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend) + 2 * (max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend))) - atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))), 180), round=clamp(0.95 * (1 - pow(max(1 - max($lean, 0) / 100, 0), 1.74)) - 0.62 * max(-$lean, 0) / 19, -1, 1), round_min=-1, round_max=1, lumbar=$round, lumbar_min=-1, lumbar_max=1, thoracic=$round, thoracic_min=-1, thoracic_max=1, side=none, side_min=-$rig_side_room * 5 / $rig_chest_ratio, side_max=$rig_side_room * 5 / $rig_chest_ratio, chest_tilt=$side * $rig_chest_ratio, chest_tilt_min=-5 * $rig_side_room, chest_tilt_max=5 * $rig_side_room, twist=none, twist_min=-($rig_twist1 + $rig_twist2 + $rig_twist3 + $rig_twist4 + $rig_twist5), twist_max=$rig_twist1 + $rig_twist2 + $rig_twist3 + $rig_twist4 + $rig_twist5, rig_flex=18.0, rig_extend=6.0, rig_twist1=3.0, rig_twist2=3.0, rig_twist3=3.0, rig_twist4=12.5, rig_twist5=12.5, rig_l0=4.293, rig_l1=7.455, rig_l2=7.551, rig_l3=9.226, rig_l4=13.841, rig_l5=17.242, rig_b0=-2.911, rig_b1=13.007, rig_b2=5.677, rig_b3=-3.822, rig_b4=-12.357, rig_b5=-8.482, rig_rest_tilt=-3.8047, rig_chest_ratio=1.558, rig_side_room=6.0, rig_hinge_back=-35.0, rig_hinge_forward=132.4) {
  if ($lumbar != none) {
    swing(spine_01, axis=fold, by=(max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend))
    swing(spine_02, axis=fold, by=(max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend))
    swing(spine_03, axis=fold, by=(max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend))
  }
  if ($thoracic != none) {
    swing(spine_04, axis=fold, by=(max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend))
    swing(spine_05, axis=fold, by=(max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend))
  }
  if ($lean != none) {
    if ($lumbar != none) {
      if ($thoracic != none) {
        $BackHinge(lean=$lean, bl=(max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend), bt=(max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend), rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
      } else {
        $BackHinge(lean=$lean, bl=(max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend), bt=0, rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
      }
    } else {
      if ($thoracic != none) {
        $BackHinge(lean=$lean, bl=0, bt=(max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend), rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
      } else {
        $BackHinge(lean=$lean, bl=0, bt=0, rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
      }
    }
  } else {
    if ($lumbar != none) {
      if ($thoracic != none) {
        $BackHinge(lean=$rig_rest_tilt, bl=(max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend), bt=(max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend), rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
      } else {
        $BackHinge(lean=$rig_rest_tilt, bl=(max($lumbar, 0) * $rig_flex + min($lumbar, 0) * $rig_extend), bt=0, rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
      }
    } else {
      if ($thoracic != none) {
        $BackHinge(lean=$rig_rest_tilt, bl=0, bt=(max($thoracic, 0) * $rig_flex + min($thoracic, 0) * $rig_extend), rig_rest_tilt=$rig_rest_tilt, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
      }
    }
  }
  if ($side != none) {
    if ($chest_tilt != none) {
      $BackSide(side=$side, chest=$chest_tilt, rig_side_room=$rig_side_room, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
    } else {
      $BackSide(side=$side, chest=$side * $rig_chest_ratio, rig_side_room=$rig_side_room, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
    }
  } else {
    if ($chest_tilt != none) {
      $BackSide(side=0, chest=$chest_tilt, rig_side_room=$rig_side_room, rig_l0=$rig_l0, rig_l1=$rig_l1, rig_l2=$rig_l2, rig_l3=$rig_l3, rig_l4=$rig_l4, rig_l5=$rig_l5, rig_b0=$rig_b0, rig_b1=$rig_b1, rig_b2=$rig_b2, rig_b3=$rig_b3, rig_b4=$rig_b4, rig_b5=$rig_b5)
    }
  }
  if ($twist != none) {
    swing(spine_01, axis=twist, by=$twist * $rig_twist1 / ($rig_twist1 + $rig_twist2 + $rig_twist3 + $rig_twist4 + $rig_twist5))
    swing(spine_02, axis=twist, by=$twist * $rig_twist2 / ($rig_twist1 + $rig_twist2 + $rig_twist3 + $rig_twist4 + $rig_twist5))
    swing(spine_03, axis=twist, by=$twist * $rig_twist3 / ($rig_twist1 + $rig_twist2 + $rig_twist3 + $rig_twist4 + $rig_twist5))
    swing(spine_04, axis=twist, by=$twist * $rig_twist4 / ($rig_twist1 + $rig_twist2 + $rig_twist3 + $rig_twist4 + $rig_twist5))
    swing(spine_05, axis=twist, by=$twist * $rig_twist5 / ($rig_twist1 + $rig_twist2 + $rig_twist3 + $rig_twist4 + $rig_twist5))
  }
}
# (helper of Back, not listed) the hinge: the pelvis folds lean less the tilt the curve alone gives the line (each segment turned
# by the bends below it, the line re-measured), counted from the rest tilt.
BackHinge = pose(lean=0.0, bl=0.0, bt=0.0, rig_rest_tilt=0.0, rig_l0=1.0, rig_l1=1.0, rig_l2=1.0, rig_l3=1.0, rig_l4=1.0, rig_l5=1.0, rig_b0=0.0, rig_b1=0.0, rig_b2=0.0, rig_b3=0.0, rig_b4=0.0, rig_b5=0.0) {
  swing(pelvis, axis=fold, by=$lean - $rig_rest_tilt - (atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1 + $bl) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2 + 2 * $bl) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3 + 3 * $bl) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4 + 3 * $bl + $bt) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5 + 3 * $bl + 2 * $bt), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1 + $bl) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2 + 2 * $bl) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3 + 3 * $bl) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4 + 3 * $bl + $bt) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5 + 3 * $bl + 2 * $bt)) - atan2($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), $rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))))
}
# (helper of Back, not listed) the side bend: a per joint on spine_01..03 and c on spine_04..05 with 3a + 2c = chest and the line
# tipped by side (a * the heights above the lower joints + c * those above the upper = side * the line's length, small angles);
# c is held to the upper joints' side room (rig_side_room) and a re-solved, so past that room the line keeps side and the
# shoulders' roll stops where the rig stops it (without the hold the upper joints' clamp turned chest_tilt=15 into -3.3);
# the rig's side axis leans LEFT, so the swings carry the flip.
BackSide = pose(side=0.0, chest=0.0, rig_side_room=6.0, rig_l0=1.0, rig_l1=1.0, rig_l2=1.0, rig_l3=1.0, rig_l4=1.0, rig_l5=1.0, rig_b0=0.0, rig_b1=0.0, rig_b2=0.0, rig_b3=0.0, rig_b4=0.0, rig_b5=0.0) {
  swing(spine_01, axis=side, by=-(($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - clamp(($chest - 3 * (($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - $chest * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) / 2) / ((($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) - 1.5 * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))) / 2, -$rig_side_room, $rig_side_room) * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))) / (($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))
  swing(spine_02, axis=side, by=-(($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - clamp(($chest - 3 * (($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - $chest * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) / 2) / ((($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) - 1.5 * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))) / 2, -$rig_side_room, $rig_side_room) * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))) / (($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))
  swing(spine_03, axis=side, by=-(($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - clamp(($chest - 3 * (($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - $chest * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) / 2) / ((($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) - 1.5 * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))) / 2, -$rig_side_room, $rig_side_room) * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))) / (($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))
  swing(spine_04, axis=side, by=-(clamp(($chest - 3 * (($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - $chest * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) / 2) / ((($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) - 1.5 * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))) / 2, -$rig_side_room, $rig_side_room)))
  swing(spine_05, axis=side, by=-(clamp(($chest - 3 * (($side * sqrt(pow($rig_l0 * sin($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * sin($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * sin($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * sin($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * sin($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * sin($rig_b5), 2) + pow($rig_l0 * cos($rig_b0) + $rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5), 2)) - $chest * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) / 2) / ((($rig_l1 * cos($rig_b1) + $rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l2 * cos($rig_b2) + $rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l3 * cos($rig_b3) + $rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5))) - 1.5 * (($rig_l4 * cos($rig_b4) + $rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)) + ($rig_l5 * cos($rig_b5)))))) / 2, -$rig_side_room, $rig_side_room)))
}

# =====================================================================================================================
# HEAD (first layer, not sided): neck_01, neck_02, head on fold, side, twist, and the look. Counted against the CHEST
# (spine_05): over a leaning or rounded Back the head follows the chest bone unless level is written.
#  turn      degrees, the face turned to the figure's RIGHT against the chest (below 0 left). Measured -75.5 .. 75.5.
#  nod       degrees, chin DOWN against the chest (below 0 chin up). Measured -84.4 .. 55.7.
#  tilt      degrees, the ear toward the RIGHT shoulder against the chest. Measured -50.3 .. 50.3 alone, about 21 at turn 70
#            with nod 40 (the side joints' stops; the build names them).
#            Any one of turn, nod, tilt, level written asks the face's direction; then the others not written are 0.
#  level     0..1, how far the face rights itself in the figure's frame (character), pitch, yaw and roll: 0 it rides the chest,
#            1 turn/nod/tilt count in the figure's frame, so a leaning back no longer tips the face; held exactly between.
#            Not written: the head follows the chest (level 0).
#  jut       -1..1, the head carried forward of the chest with the face's direction kept: 1 as far forward as the neck goes
#            (+3.2 cm on this rig), -1 tucked back as far as it goes (-2.6 cm). Not written: not asked.
#  look_at   a place ($Place) the face turns to, written last, so it takes the face's direction over turn/nod/tilt (a look
#            and turn/nod do not add: the later line wins). Not written: not asked.
#  rig_tw_*, rig_sd_*   what twist and side each neck joint needs for a pure turn and tilt (this rig couples them: 10 of twist
#            also tilts 5.8, 10 of side also turns 4.0); rig_tilt_per_turn_nod the tilt a turn and nod together add;
#            rig_share_*   the three joints' shares (the rig gives them equal room); rig_jut_forward / rig_jut_back the
#            head's counter-fold at jut 1 / -1 (27.9 = neck_01's forward room 18.6 over its 2/3 share; 18.6 the head's
#            forward room); rig_jut_neck_01 the neck_01's share of that fold (2/3; neck_02 takes the rest).
#  Worked values (built): a turned, nodded, tilted head $Head(turn=70, nod=40, tilt=30) -> 70.04 / 40.06 / 21.06 (the
#              side joints' stop, said); a chin tuck $Head(jut=-1) -> the head 2.57 cm back, face unchanged; over a hunch
#              (Back lean 45, round 0.8: the chest 74.2 down) $Head(level=1) -> face 0.00 in the room, level=0.5 -> 37.10.
Head = pose(turn=none, turn_min=-75.5, turn_max=75.5, nod=none, nod_min=-84.4, nod_max=55.7, tilt=none, tilt_min=-50.3, tilt_max=50.3, level=none, level_min=0, level_max=1, jut=none, jut_min=-1, jut_max=1, look_at=none, rig_tw_turn=0.9964, rig_tw_tilt=-0.1362, rig_sd_turn=-0.1958, rig_sd_tilt=-0.9882, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=0.0055, rig_share_neck_01=0.3333, rig_share_neck_02=0.3333, rig_share_head=0.3334, rig_jut_forward=27.9, rig_jut_back=18.6, rig_jut_neck_01=0.6667) {
  if ($turn != none) {
    if ($nod != none) {
      if ($tilt != none) {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=$nod, tilt=$tilt, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        } else {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=$nod, tilt=$tilt, level=0, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      } else {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=$nod, tilt=0, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        } else {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=$nod, tilt=0, level=0, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      }
    } else {
      if ($tilt != none) {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=0, tilt=$tilt, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        } else {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=0, tilt=$tilt, level=0, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      } else {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=0, tilt=0, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        } else {
          $HeadDir(turn=$turn, nod=0, tilt=0, level=0, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      }
    }
  } else {
    if ($nod != none) {
      if ($tilt != none) {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=0, nod=$nod, tilt=$tilt, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        } else {
          $HeadDir(turn=0, nod=$nod, tilt=$tilt, level=0, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      } else {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=0, nod=$nod, tilt=0, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        } else {
          $HeadDir(turn=0, nod=$nod, tilt=0, level=0, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      }
    } else {
      if ($tilt != none) {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=0, nod=0, tilt=$tilt, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        } else {
          $HeadDir(turn=0, nod=0, tilt=$tilt, level=0, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      } else {
        if ($level != none) {
          $HeadDir(turn=0, nod=0, tilt=0, level=$level, rig_tw_turn=$rig_tw_turn, rig_tw_tilt=$rig_tw_tilt, rig_sd_turn=$rig_sd_turn, rig_sd_tilt=$rig_sd_tilt, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=$rig_tilt_per_turn_nod, rig_share_neck_01=$rig_share_neck_01, rig_share_neck_02=$rig_share_neck_02, rig_share_head=$rig_share_head)
        }
      }
    }
  }
  if ($jut != none) {
    swing(neck_01, axis=fold, by=(max($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_forward + min($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_back) * $rig_jut_neck_01)
    swing(neck_02, axis=fold, by=(max($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_forward + min($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_back) * (1 - $rig_jut_neck_01))
    swing(head, axis=fold, by=-(max($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_forward + min($jut, 0) * $rig_jut_back))
  }
  if ($look_at != none) {
    aim($Look, from=$Face, at=$look_at)
  }
}
# (helper of Head, not listed) the face's direction: swings with the couplings undone, then an aim against the chest
# (weight 1 - level) and one in the figure's frame (weight level) that also holds the roll.
HeadDir = pose(turn=0.0, nod=0.0, tilt=0.0, level=0.0, rig_tw_turn=1.0, rig_tw_tilt=0.0, rig_sd_turn=0.0, rig_sd_tilt=-1.0, rig_tilt_per_turn_nod=0.0, rig_share_neck_01=0.3333, rig_share_neck_02=0.3333, rig_share_head=0.3333) {
  swing(neck_01, axis=twist, by=($turn * $rig_tw_turn + ($tilt + $rig_tilt_per_turn_nod * $turn * $nod) * $rig_tw_tilt) * $rig_share_neck_01)
  swing(neck_01, axis=fold, by=$nod * $rig_share_neck_01)
  swing(neck_01, axis=side, by=($turn * $rig_sd_turn + ($tilt + $rig_tilt_per_turn_nod * $turn * $nod) * $rig_sd_tilt) * $rig_share_neck_01)
  swing(neck_02, axis=twist, by=($turn * $rig_tw_turn + ($tilt + $rig_tilt_per_turn_nod * $turn * $nod) * $rig_tw_tilt) * $rig_share_neck_02)
  swing(neck_02, axis=fold, by=$nod * $rig_share_neck_02)
  swing(neck_02, axis=side, by=($turn * $rig_sd_turn + ($tilt + $rig_tilt_per_turn_nod * $turn * $nod) * $rig_sd_tilt) * $rig_share_neck_02)
  swing(head, axis=twist, by=($turn * $rig_tw_turn + ($tilt + $rig_tilt_per_turn_nod * $turn * $nod) * $rig_tw_tilt) * $rig_share_head)
  swing(head, axis=fold, by=$nod * $rig_share_head)
  swing(head, axis=side, by=($turn * $rig_sd_turn + ($tilt + $rig_tilt_per_turn_nod * $turn * $nod) * $rig_sd_tilt) * $rig_share_head)
  aim($LookH, from=$Face, toward=(forward, right=$turn, down=$nod), relative=spine_05, weight=1 - $level)
  aim($LookL, from=$Face, toward=(forward, right=$turn, down=$nod), up=(up, right=$tilt), relative=character, weight=$level)
}

# =====================================================================================================================
# UPPERARM (first layer, sided): the collar bone (clavicle fold and side) and where the upper arm points (upperarm aim). The upper
# arm's own turn is fixed by its direction and the forearm's (no roll).
#  raise, azimuth  where the upper arm (shoulder to elbow) points: raise 0 straight down, 90 level, 180 up; azimuth 0 ahead, 90
#            out to its own side, 180 behind, below 0 across; counted in frame. Either one written asks the direction: raise
#            alone takes azimuth 0, azimuth alone takes the rig's rest raise (rig_rest_raise 12.67). Neither: not asked, the arm
#            rides the chest. Measured: every built direction exact (0.0); forward to 175, to the side to 170 with the collar
#            bone following (162 without); behind the side (azimuth 130) the shoulder's stop names the shortfall.
#  shrug     -1..1, the shoulder joint raised (1 = the collar's 45 up, 12.7 cm), below 0 pressed down (its 15). Not written,
#            follows raise: 0.13 * (raise - rest) / (120 - rest), rising on past 120 (0.19 at 170) and faded to 0 between 170 and 180
#            (rig_fade_start/end: past 172 the shoulder's stop is met sooner with the collar raised). A shrug above 0 eases the
#            arm out by rig_shrug_ease (10) * shrug^2 * cos(raise) degrees, so a hanging arm clears the ribs under a full
#            shrug (the shrug that follows raise eases it 0.03 at most: raise reads exact).
#  shoulder_forward  -1..1, the shoulder joint rolled forward (the collar's 17.5, 5.3 cm), below 0 drawn back. Not written,
#            follows raise and azimuth: -0.91 * (the same share as shrug) * (0.5 + azimuth / 90), azimuth held to 0..90 (the
#            source gives no factor outside it), held to -1..1 and faded as shrug.
#  frame     what the directions count from: character (default; a leaning back does not tip them) or a bone (spine_05 = the
#            chest).   left, right   sides.
#  rig_up_deg, rig_down_deg, rig_forward_deg, rig_back_deg   the collar bone's room from rest (45, 15, 17.5, 17.5).
#  Worked values (built): arms out level $UpperArm(raise=90, azimuth=90) -> 90.00 / 90.00, collar 4.07 up; one arm up to
#              the side $UpperArm(raise=170, azimuth=90) -> 170.00 (the collar 8.29 up, 17.5 back; without it 162.22); a forward
#              raise $UpperArm(raise=60) -> 60.02 / 0.00. Uneven: $UpperArm(raise=90, azimuth=90, right=false)
#              $UpperArm(raise=30, azimuth=45, left=false). Worst: raise 175 to the side reads 161.1 (the collar's fade).
UpperArm = pose(raise=none, raise_min=0, raise_max=175, azimuth=0 * $raise, azimuth_min=-180, azimuth_max=180, shrug=0.13 * max($raise - $rig_rest_raise, 0) / (120 - $rig_rest_raise) * (clamp(($rig_fade_end - $raise) / ($rig_fade_end - $rig_fade_start), 0, 1)), shrug_min=-1, shrug_max=1, shoulder_forward=clamp(-0.91 * (clamp(($raise - $rig_rest_raise) / (120 - $rig_rest_raise), 0, 1)) * (0.5 + clamp($azimuth, 0, 90) / 90), -1, 1) * (clamp(($rig_fade_end - $raise) / ($rig_fade_end - $rig_fade_start), 0, 1)), shoulder_forward_min=-1, shoulder_forward_max=1, frame=character, left=true, right=true, rig_rest_raise=12.67, rig_up_deg=45.0, rig_down_deg=15.0, rig_forward_deg=17.5, rig_back_deg=17.5, rig_fade_start=170.0, rig_fade_end=180.0, rig_shrug_ease=10.0) {
  if ($shrug != none) {
    if ($right) { swing(clavicle_r, axis=fold, by=(max($shrug, 0) * $rig_up_deg + min($shrug, 0) * $rig_down_deg)) }
    if ($left) { swing(clavicle_l, axis=fold, by=(max($shrug, 0) * $rig_up_deg + min($shrug, 0) * $rig_down_deg)) }
  }
  if ($shoulder_forward != none) {
    if ($right) { swing(clavicle_r, axis=side, by=(max($shoulder_forward, 0) * $rig_forward_deg + min($shoulder_forward, 0) * $rig_back_deg)) }
    if ($left) { swing(clavicle_l, axis=side, by=(max($shoulder_forward, 0) * $rig_forward_deg + min($shoulder_forward, 0) * $rig_back_deg)) }
  }
  if ($raise != none) {
    if ($azimuth != none) {
      if ($shrug != none) {
        $UpperArmDir(raise=$raise, azimuth=$azimuth, lift=$shrug, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right, rig_shrug_ease=$rig_shrug_ease)
      } else {
        $UpperArmDir(raise=$raise, azimuth=$azimuth, lift=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right, rig_shrug_ease=$rig_shrug_ease)
      }
    } else {
      if ($shrug != none) {
        $UpperArmDir(raise=$raise, azimuth=0, lift=$shrug, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right, rig_shrug_ease=$rig_shrug_ease)
      } else {
        $UpperArmDir(raise=$raise, azimuth=0, lift=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right, rig_shrug_ease=$rig_shrug_ease)
      }
    }
  } else {
    if ($azimuth != none) {
      if ($shrug != none) {
        $UpperArmDir(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$azimuth, lift=$shrug, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right, rig_shrug_ease=$rig_shrug_ease)
      } else {
        $UpperArmDir(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$azimuth, lift=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right, rig_shrug_ease=$rig_shrug_ease)
      }
    }
  }
}
# (helper of UpperArm, not listed) the aim, each side in its own block; the left line carries the flip (left=).
UpperArmDir = pose(raise=0.0, azimuth=0.0, lift=0.0, frame=character, left=true, right=true, rig_shrug_ease=0.0) {
  if ($right) { aim(upperarm_r, from=$UpperArmR, toward=(down, forward=atan2(sin(($raise + $rig_shrug_ease * pow(max($lift, 0), 2) * max(cos($raise), 0))) * cos($azimuth), cos(($raise + $rig_shrug_ease * pow(max($lift, 0), 2) * max(cos($raise), 0)))), right=asin(sin(($raise + $rig_shrug_ease * pow(max($lift, 0), 2) * max(cos($raise), 0))) * sin($azimuth))), relative=$frame) }
  if ($left) { aim(upperarm_l, from=$UpperArmL, toward=(down, forward=atan2(sin(($raise + $rig_shrug_ease * pow(max($lift, 0), 2) * max(cos($raise), 0))) * cos($azimuth), cos(($raise + $rig_shrug_ease * pow(max($lift, 0), 2) * max(cos($raise), 0)))), left=asin(sin(($raise + $rig_shrug_ease * pow(max($lift, 0), 2) * max(cos($raise), 0))) * sin($azimuth))), relative=$frame) }
}

# FOREARM (first layer, sided): where the forearm points and where its palm faces (lowerarm aim; its turn about its length
# comes from the palm). The wrist and fingers are the Hand's.
#  raise, azimuth  where the forearm (elbow to wrist) points, ABSOLUTE in frame (not counted from the upper arm); the pair rule
#            as UpperArm's (azimuth alone takes rig_rest_raise 18.05). Neither: the forearm rides the upper arm. Met within 0.3
#            wherever the elbow (0 to 150 bent) and the shoulder's twist (+-73.8) can bring it; elsewhere the build says
#            "'lowerarm_r' could not be turned ... N short".
#  palm_raise, palm_azimuth  where the PALM faces, in the same two-angle language and the same numbers on both arms: raise 0
#            the palm faces down, 180 up; 90 with azimuth -90 faces in (toward the body's middle), 90 out, 0 ahead. The pair rule
#            as above (palm_azimuth alone takes rig_rest_palm_raise). A palm facing along the forearm has no meaning (the aim's
#            up is taken square to the forearm). Neither written: the forearm's turn is not asked. A palm written with no
#            forearm direction holds the forearm at its rest direction (rig_rest_raise, rig_rest_azimuth 44.11) in frame:
#            the build takes a palm only with a direction ("aim(up=) ... needs toward= as well").
#  frame, left, right  as UpperArm's.
#  Measured: the palm is held exactly where the forearm's twist (+-90.6) can turn it; past it the build says "'lowerarm_r'
#              is turned N short of its up=". Worked values (built), the upper arm at (45, 45) unless said: forearm level ahead,
#              palm down $Forearm(raise=90, azimuth=0, palm_raise=0) -> 90.03 / 0.04, palm 0.03; palm in and 45 down
#              $Forearm(raise=90, azimuth=0, palm_raise=45, palm_azimuth=-90) -> palm 45.00 / -89.93; arms out, palms forward
#              $UpperArm(raise=90, azimuth=90) $Forearm(raise=90, azimuth=90, palm_raise=90, palm_azimuth=0) -> palm 90.00 / 0.00.
Forearm = pose(raise=none, raise_min=0, raise_max=180, azimuth=0 * $raise, azimuth_min=-180, azimuth_max=180, palm_raise=none, palm_raise_min=0, palm_raise_max=180, palm_azimuth=0 * $palm_raise, palm_azimuth_min=-180, palm_azimuth_max=180, frame=character, left=true, right=true, rig_rest_raise=18.05, rig_rest_azimuth=44.11, rig_rest_palm_raise=77.76) {
  if ($raise != none) {
    if ($azimuth != none) {
      if ($palm_raise != none) {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$raise, azimuth=$azimuth, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        } else {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$raise, azimuth=$azimuth, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      } else {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$raise, azimuth=$azimuth, palm_raise=$rig_rest_palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        } else {
          $ForearmAim(raise=$raise, azimuth=$azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      }
    } else {
      if ($palm_raise != none) {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$raise, azimuth=0, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        } else {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$raise, azimuth=0, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      } else {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$raise, azimuth=0, palm_raise=$rig_rest_palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        } else {
          $ForearmAim(raise=$raise, azimuth=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      }
    }
  } else {
    if ($azimuth != none) {
      if ($palm_raise != none) {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$azimuth, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        } else {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$azimuth, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      } else {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$azimuth, palm_raise=$rig_rest_palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        } else {
          $ForearmAim(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      }
    } else {
      if ($palm_raise != none) {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_rest_azimuth, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        } else {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_rest_azimuth, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=0, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      } else {
        if ($palm_azimuth != none) {
          $ForearmAimPalm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_rest_azimuth, palm_raise=$rig_rest_palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
# (helpers of Forearm, not listed) the aim with a direction, and with a direction and the palm.
ForearmAim = pose(raise=0.0, azimuth=0.0, frame=character, left=true, right=true) {
  if ($right) { aim(lowerarm_r, from=$ForeR, toward=(down, forward=atan2(sin($raise) * cos($azimuth), cos($raise)), right=asin(sin($raise) * sin($azimuth))), relative=$frame) }
  if ($left) { aim(lowerarm_l, from=$ForeL, toward=(down, forward=atan2(sin($raise) * cos($azimuth), cos($raise)), left=asin(sin($raise) * sin($azimuth))), relative=$frame) }
}
ForearmAimPalm = pose(raise=0.0, azimuth=0.0, palm_raise=90.0, palm_azimuth=0.0, frame=character, left=true, right=true) {
  if ($right) { aim(lowerarm_r, from=$ForeR, toward=(down, forward=atan2(sin($raise) * cos($azimuth), cos($raise)), right=asin(sin($raise) * sin($azimuth))), up=(down, forward=atan2(sin($palm_raise) * cos($palm_azimuth), cos($palm_raise)), right=asin(sin($palm_raise) * sin($palm_azimuth))), relative=$frame) }
  if ($left) { aim(lowerarm_l, from=$ForeL, toward=(down, forward=atan2(sin($raise) * cos($azimuth), cos($raise)), left=asin(sin($raise) * sin($azimuth))), up=(down, forward=atan2(sin($palm_raise) * cos($palm_azimuth), cos($palm_raise)), left=asin(sin($palm_raise) * sin($palm_azimuth))), relative=$frame) }
}

# ARMREACH (second layer, sided: calls only UpperArm and Forearm): the arm along a line from the shoulder and how far out.
#  raise, azimuth  the direction from the shoulder joint to the wrist (hand joint), as UpperArm's; the pair rule (azimuth alone
#            takes rig_rest_raise 14.72, the rest line's). Neither written: no line asked (the palm still passes on).
#  reach     the wrist's distance along that line as a share of rig_upper_len + rig_fore_len (55.8 cm): 1 (default) the arm
#            straight. Measured 0.259 (the elbow's 150 stop) to 1; above 1 refused by the arithmetic ("sqrt() ... needs a value
#            of zero or more").
#  swivel    degrees the elbow is swung round that line from its LOWEST place, + out then up; default 0. A bent arm near the
#            trunk needs it written (the guard built only from 30 up: 0 and 20 put the forearm in the chest).
#  palm_raise, palm_azimuth  passed on to Forearm.   frame, left, right   as UpperArm's.
#  shoulder_forward  -1..1, how open the shoulder is: below 0 the shoulder drawn back (the chest opens), above 0 rolled
#            forward, about 5 cm each way at the ends. Not written: it follows the arm's raise and azimuth as UpperArm's does.
#  shrug     -1..1, the shoulder raised (above 0) or pressed down (below 0). Not written: it follows the raise as UpperArm's.
#            Both are passed to UpperArm; they act with a direction written (raise or azimuth), as the rest of the arm does.
#  Arithmetic: the elbow's direction u = ca * D + sqrt(1 - ca^2) * n (D the line, ca by the law of cosines from reach and the two
#  lengths, n the lowest perpendicular swung by swivel); the forearm is the line from the elbow to the wrist.
#  Worked values (built): a T pose $ArmReach(raise=90, azimuth=90) -> line 90.00 / 90.00, reach 1.003; a zombie's reach
#              $ArmReach(raise=80, azimuth=5, reach=0.95) -> 80.10 / 4.98, reach 0.953; a bent arm $ArmReach(raise=90,
#              azimuth=30, reach=0.4) -> 90.62 / 30.22, reach 0.401.
ArmReach = pose(raise=none, raise_min=0, raise_max=180, azimuth=0 * $raise, azimuth_min=-180, azimuth_max=180, reach=1.0, reach_min=0.26, reach_max=1, swivel=0.0, swivel_min=-60, swivel_max=150, palm_raise=none, palm_raise_min=0, palm_raise_max=180, palm_azimuth=0 * $palm_raise, palm_azimuth_min=-180, palm_azimuth_max=180, shrug=none, shrug_min=-1, shrug_max=1, shoulder_forward=none, shoulder_forward_min=-1, shoulder_forward_max=1, frame=character, left=true, right=true, rig_upper_len=28.4, rig_fore_len=27.4, rig_rest_raise=14.72) {
  if ($raise != none) {
    if ($azimuth != none) {
      $ArmReachElbow(raise=$raise, azimuth=$azimuth, swivel=$swivel, d=$reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len), ca=($rig_upper_len * $rig_upper_len + pow($reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len), 2) - $rig_fore_len * $rig_fore_len) / (2 * $rig_upper_len * $reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len)), rig_upper_len=$rig_upper_len, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, shrug=$shrug, shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    } else {
      $ArmReachElbow(raise=$raise, azimuth=0, swivel=$swivel, d=$reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len), ca=($rig_upper_len * $rig_upper_len + pow($reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len), 2) - $rig_fore_len * $rig_fore_len) / (2 * $rig_upper_len * $reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len)), rig_upper_len=$rig_upper_len, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, shrug=$shrug, shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    }
  } else {
    if ($azimuth != none) {
      $ArmReachElbow(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$azimuth, swivel=$swivel, d=$reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len), ca=($rig_upper_len * $rig_upper_len + pow($reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len), 2) - $rig_fore_len * $rig_fore_len) / (2 * $rig_upper_len * $reach * ($rig_upper_len + $rig_fore_len)), rig_upper_len=$rig_upper_len, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, shrug=$shrug, shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    } else {
      $Forearm(palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    }
  }
}
# (helper of ArmReach, not listed) the elbow's direction u (side-local: out, forward, up) and the wrist's place w from the shoulder.
ArmReachElbow = pose(raise=90.0, azimuth=0.0, swivel=0.0, d=40.0, ca=0.7, rig_upper_len=28.4, palm_raise=none, palm_azimuth=none, shrug=none, shoulder_forward=none, frame=character, left=true, right=true) {
  $ArmReachAim(ux=$ca * sin($raise) * sin($azimuth) + sqrt(1 - $ca * $ca + 0.000000001) * (sin($swivel) * cos($azimuth) - cos($swivel) * cos($raise) * sin($azimuth)), uy=$ca * sin($raise) * cos($azimuth) - sqrt(1 - $ca * $ca + 0.000000001) * (sin($swivel) * sin($azimuth) + cos($swivel) * cos($raise) * cos($azimuth)), uz=-$ca * cos($raise) - sqrt(1 - $ca * $ca + 0.000000001) * cos($swivel) * sin($raise), wx=$d * sin($raise) * sin($azimuth), wy=$d * sin($raise) * cos($azimuth), wz=-$d * cos($raise), rig_upper_len=$rig_upper_len, palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, shrug=$shrug, shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
}
# (helper of ArmReach, not listed) the two directions back into raise/azimuth, handed to the first layer.
ArmReachAim = pose(ux=0.0, uy=0.7, uz=-0.7, wx=0.0, wy=40.0, wz=0.0, rig_upper_len=28.4, palm_raise=none, palm_azimuth=none, shrug=none, shoulder_forward=none, frame=character, left=true, right=true) {
  if ($shrug != none) {
    if ($shoulder_forward != none) {
      $UpperArm(raise=atan2(sqrt($ux * $ux + $uy * $uy), -$uz), azimuth=atan2($ux, $uy), shrug=$shrug, shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    } else {
      $UpperArm(raise=atan2(sqrt($ux * $ux + $uy * $uy), -$uz), azimuth=atan2($ux, $uy), shrug=$shrug, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    }
  } else {
    if ($shoulder_forward != none) {
      $UpperArm(raise=atan2(sqrt($ux * $ux + $uy * $uy), -$uz), azimuth=atan2($ux, $uy), shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    } else {
      $UpperArm(raise=atan2(sqrt($ux * $ux + $uy * $uy), -$uz), azimuth=atan2($ux, $uy), frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
    }
  }
  $Forearm(raise=atan2(sqrt(pow($wx - $rig_upper_len * $ux, 2) + pow($wy - $rig_upper_len * $uy, 2)), $rig_upper_len * $uz - $wz), azimuth=atan2($wx - $rig_upper_len * $ux, $wy - $rig_upper_len * $uy), palm_raise=$palm_raise, palm_azimuth=$palm_azimuth, frame=$frame, left=$left, right=$right)
}

# HANG (second layer, sided: calls UpperArm and Forearm): the arms hanging at the rig's rest directions in the figure's frame, so a
# bow or a slump says "the arms hang" without the rest numbers, and the shoulders' values pass down.
#  shrug, shoulder_forward   passed to UpperArm (not written: the collar bone follows the arm's raise, which at rest is 0).
#  left, right   sides.   rig_rest_raise/azimuth (12.67, 77.17), rig_fore_rest_raise/azimuth (18.05, 44.11): the rest hang.
#  Worked values (built): $Hang -> rest exactly; under $Back(lean=45) the arms keep 12.67 / 77.17 in the room (the wrist
#              moves with the shoulder, 39.3 cm); a full shrug $Hang(shrug=1) builds: collar 43.87 up, the upper arm eased out to
#              22.43, nothing in the ribs (as two presets it was refused, the forearm 2.2 cm into spine_03).
Hang = pose(shrug=none, shrug_min=-1, shrug_max=1, shoulder_forward=none, shoulder_forward_min=-1, shoulder_forward_max=1, left=true, right=true, rig_rest_raise=12.67, rig_rest_azimuth=77.17, rig_fore_rest_raise=18.05, rig_fore_rest_azimuth=44.11) {
  if ($shrug != none) {
    if ($shoulder_forward != none) {
      $UpperArm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_rest_azimuth, shrug=$shrug, shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, left=$left, right=$right)
    } else {
      $UpperArm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_rest_azimuth, shrug=$shrug, left=$left, right=$right)
    }
  } else {
    if ($shoulder_forward != none) {
      $UpperArm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_rest_azimuth, shoulder_forward=$shoulder_forward, left=$left, right=$right)
    } else {
      $UpperArm(raise=$rig_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_rest_azimuth, left=$left, right=$right)
    }
  }
  $Forearm(raise=$rig_fore_rest_raise, azimuth=$rig_fore_rest_azimuth, left=$left, right=$right)
}

# =====================================================================================================================
# HIPS (first layer, not sided): the pelvis only: lowered, moved, turned and hiked. A standing pose gets these from Stance, which
# works them out from the feet; written alone, the feet go with the pelvis (nothing holds them).
#  drop      of leg length (rig_leg 86.2 cm): the pelvis lowered; below 0 raised. Not written: not asked.
#  shift_right, shift_forward   cm: the pelvis moved to the figure's right / forward. Not written: not asked.
#  hike      degrees: the RIGHT hip higher (about the figure's front-to-back axis). Not written: not asked.
#  turn      degrees: the pelvis turned to the figure's right about the vertical. Not written: not asked.
#  rig_pelvis_yaw   the pelvis bone's rest turn off the figure's axes (2.06): the two swing axes are worked from it.
#  Worked values (built): $Hips -> writes nothing; $Hips(drop=0.1) alone -> the pelvis 8.62 cm down and the feet with it
#              (write Stance); through Stance: turn 30 -> the hip line 30.00, hike 6 -> 6.00.
Hips = pose(drop=none, drop_min=-0.169, drop_max=0.5, shift_right=none, shift_right_min=-54, shift_right_max=54, shift_forward=none, shift_forward_min=-129.7, shift_forward_max=127.9, hike=none, hike_min=-30, hike_max=30, turn=none, turn_min=-60, turn_max=60, rig_leg=86.2, rig_pelvis_yaw=2.06) {
  if ($drop != none) { shift(pelvis, toward=down, by=$drop * $rig_leg) }
  if ($shift_right != none) { shift(pelvis, toward=right, by=$shift_right) }
  if ($shift_forward != none) { shift(pelvis, toward=forward, by=$shift_forward) }
  if ($turn != none) { swing(pelvis, axis=(cos($rig_pelvis_yaw), -sin($rig_pelvis_yaw), 0), by=$turn) }
  if ($hike != none) { swing(pelvis, axis=(sin($rig_pelvis_yaw), cos($rig_pelvis_yaw), 0), by=$hike) }
}

# FOOTAT (first layer, sided): a planted foot, POSED (no plant, reach or balance): thigh, calf, foot and ball of that leg, each
# turned by an aim worked out from where the foot stands and where the pelvis is. Calling it stands the foot: a value not written
# is the rest place (forward, out) or 0 (turnout, knee_out, heel), as a planted foot needs a place.
#  forward   of leg length: the ankle ahead of its hip as it stands at rest; below 0 behind. Rest rig_rest_forward -0.0293.
#  out       of hip width (rig_hip_width 20.04 cm): the ankle out to its own side from under its hip; below 0 across. Rest
#            rig_rest_out 0.1954.
#  turnout   degrees: the toes out to its own side; below 0 in. 0 the rest heading.
#  knee_out  degrees: the knee swung out round the hip-to-ankle line; 0 the knee over the foot's line.
#  heel      degrees, the sole's angle from the floor: above 0 the heel lifted (the foot turns about its ball, the ankle rises by
#            what that lifts); below 0 on the heel, toes up. The heel ALSO lifts by itself where the ankle runs out of room (the
#            shin past rig_ankle_room over the foot) or the leg out of length: written as the case it is (FootAtBend1).
#  px, py, pz, hike, turn   the pelvis's place (cm: x left, y forward, z up) and turns, as Hips was given them: passed by Stance;
#            0 = the rest pelvis.   left, right   sides.
#  rig_*_r / rig_*_l   each leg's rest measures (thigh, shin, the ankle's height, the ankle-to-ball run and drop, the foot's rest
#            heading, the heel point, the ankle's rest angle, the toes' rest direction); the common rig_ values the hip joints'
#            place on the pelvis, the leg's length and the ankle's room (37 = the rig's 39 less 2).
#  Nothing holds the foot: it stands where the arithmetic puts it, given the pelvis Stance passes; a foot out of reach FLOATS
#  and nothing says so.
#  Worked values (built): $FootAt -> rest (knees 0.05 / 0.09, soles 0.00); a step and a turned foot as two calls
#              $FootAt(right=false, forward=0.1) $FootAt(left=false, out=0.5, turnout=20) (under the rest pelvis the legs are
